-- BeeAware Brasil roadmap / Phase 4 — RJ Geo, CISP boundaries.
--
-- Third of three (RISP -> AISP -> CISP, this migration order matters:
-- each CISP row's parent_area_id lookup joins against AISP rows the
-- previous migration already inserted). See
-- 20260825210000_rj_risp_geometry.sql's header for the full source,
-- verification, and one-off-manual-population rationale — same source
-- page, same KML extraction, same precision/validity handling. CISP is
-- the finest tier (police-district level, 137 of them), what
-- RjIspAdapter's own per-CISP monthly counts could finally join against
-- for real district-level (not just municipality-level) statistics —
-- not wired up in this migration; this is the geometry layer only.

-- Generated from real CISP KML data (ispdados.rj.gov.br) — 137 rows.
